        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Bellman-Ford is the cleanest answer here: a few lines, no heap, and the limit is simply the number of rounds. The Dijkstra version is worth knowing for problems where the count isn't a small number of rounds."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Edge cases to test"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "**k = 0** — only direct flights count.",
        "**The cheapest route has too many stops** — the answer must be the cheapest route **within** the limit.",
        "**No route at all** — -1.",
        "**Forgetting the copy** — relaxing in place lets one round chain several flights, and k = 0 can wrongly return a two-flight price."
      ]
    },
